\section*{2. Vapor-liquid equilibrium}

Figure 9 shows that both vapor and liquid equilibrium densities obtained by the DPMD-FR and DPMD-LR models are in good agreement with the SPC/E-FW results, and no significant discrepancies exist between the two. This shows that although the DPMD-FR model has significant differences in the short-range representation so as to compensate for the lack of explicit long-range interactions, when considering the whole picture of the bulk interfacial system, the interactions add up to provide the accurate description of the equilibrium properties. It is also worth mentioning that these properties are directly related to the chemical potential of the liquid, indicating the ability of both models to reproduce this property accordingly with the SPC/E-FW model. The same is true for the

