\section*{3. Second virial coefficients}

We now observe the effects of long-range incorporation on the second virial coefficient, as shown in Fig. 10. As expected from the cluster analysis, the results for DPMD-LR are in better agreement with that of SPC/E-FW given the pairwise nature of the second virial coefficient calculation. At lower temperatures, higher discrepancies between SPC/E-FR and DPMD-LR are observed, which might indicate small differences in intermolecular energy predictions between the two models that are exacerbated through the Mayer function at those temperatures. However, these differences

